From 80d644a5ac2d27639d4c3f7ff50333a1c085a49a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:43:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: unauthenticated NAS Reject detector
 (identity-forcing)

Adds the `unauthenticated_nas_reject` analyzer: it flags an Attach/TAU/Service
Reject carrying an identity-forcing EMM cause (#9 "UE identity cannot be derived
by the network" or #10 "implicitly detached") received before a security context
is established in the attach cycle.

This closes the NAS-Reject IMSI-catching path (the "identity reveal" blind spot
the Devilray study, Oh et al. 2026, found in Rayhunter): a false base station
that cannot authenticate the UE sends such a reject, the UE deletes its GUTI and
re-attaches with its IMSI. The reject is accepted without integrity protection
before a security context exists (TS 24.301 4.4.4.2), so the analyzer tracks
`Security Mode Complete` per attach cycle and reports:
- High  when the reject is unprotected (no security context yet) -- the signal;
- Low   when it follows an established security context (likely a genuine failure
        such as an MME restart).

Scope is deliberately narrowed to #9/#10 (Devilray's reliable causes) and keyed
on security state, to stay precise. Off by default (`AnalyzerConfig` default
false) pending per-network false-positive calibration; the existing diagnostic
analyzer still logs the broader cause set informationally.

Test harness: adds `emm_message()` to `analysis::test_util` and unit tests
covering the unprotected/High, protected/Low, non-identity-cause, TAU/Service,
and cycle-reset paths.

Ref: Orbic-Rayhunter T-OR-052; ref-docs/lte-imsi-catcher-detection.md 3.2.
Signed-off-by: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
